// Spec #3147 ST-1 -- the Fredo application command manifest.
//
// This module is the ONE list handed to `tauri_build::AppManifest::commands(...)`
// in `build.rs`, and it is compiled twice on purpose:
//
//   * into the app crate (this module), where the `#[cfg(test)]` guards at the
//     bottom run, and
//   * into `build.rs` through `include!("src/runtime/command_manifest.rs")`, where
//     `tauri-build` turns every entry into an `allow-<command>` / `deny-<command>`
//     permission under `permissions/autogenerated/` (gitignored, build output).
//
// WHY THIS LIST EXISTS -- do not delete an entry to "clean up":
//
// Registering an app manifest flips Tauri's IPC authority gate on
// (`has_app_acl_manifest` becomes true), so `resolve_access` runs for EVERY
// command against EVERY window label. Two consequences are load-bearing:
//
//   1. A window that matches no capability -- the future `installed-<id>`
//      window -- gets NO command access. That refusal is the mechanism AC-2
//      depends on.
//   2. A command that is registered but absent from this manifest gets no
//      autogenerated permission, so no capability can grant it and it is denied
//      (and, under `removeUnusedCommands`, dropped) in every built-in window.
//      That is the top regression risk of this spec.
//
// The guards below cover (2) in two directions:
//
//   * `every_registered_command_is_in_the_manifest` -- parses the real
//     `generate_handler![...]` block out of `lib.rs` and asserts the SUPERSET
//     direction only (registered => listed). The reverse is deliberately NOT
//     asserted: later #3147 sub-tasks append manifest entries before they
//     register the matching handler, so a bidirectional assertion would fail
//     by construction mid-chain.
//   * `every_registered_command_is_granted_to_the_built_in_windows` -- asserts the
//     hand-authored permission set grants every registered command, and that a
//     capability references that set for the built-in window class. It keys on
//     the real registrations (not on this list) so a manifest entry appended
//     ahead of its handler is exempt until it is registered. A registered
//     command with no grant is denied at runtime to every built-in window.
//
// KEEP THIS FILE IMPORT-FREE. `build.rs` is a separate crate that
// `include!`-s it; any `use` of a parent-crate path here would break the build
// script. (The `#[cfg(test)]` module is inert there -- `cfg(test)` is not set
// for a build script.)

